WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.815
Step 1. Open the Requirements section.

1.2
00:00:02.815 --> 00:00:08.149
Here you link specimen, observation and charge item definitions to the activity

1.3
00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:12.700
definition, and choose its healthcare service and locations.

2.1
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.084
Step 2. Link specimen requirements. Select Select Specimen Requirements,

2.2
00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.791
then search for a specimen definition and select it.

2.3
00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:25.571
Repeat for each sample that the service needs.

3.1
00:00:25.571 --> 00:00:31.610
Step 3. Link observation requirements. Select Select Observation Requirements,

3.2
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:37.473
then select an observation definition for each result that the service records.

3.3
00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:40.273
You can add each one only once.

4.1
00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:43.255
Step 4. Link charge item definitions.

4.2
00:00:43.255 --> 00:00:48.570
Select Select Charge Item Definitions, and select each one that applies.

4.3
00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:51.228
When a clinician orders the service,

4.4
00:00:51.228 --> 00:00:55.345
Care creates a charge for each linked definition.

5.1
00:00:55.345 --> 00:00:59.473
Step 5. Choose the healthcare service and the locations.

5.2
00:00:59.473 --> 00:01:01.620
Healthcare Service is optional.

5.3
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:12.691
In Locations, select the locations where staff do the service.

6.1
00:01:12.691 --> 00:01:15.667
Step 6. Save the activity definition.

6.2
00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:21.045
Select Create for a new activity definition, or Save for one that exists.

6.3
00:01:21.045 --> 00:01:25.745
Care saves the requirements with the activity definition.
